	(footprint "dcu-carrier:Teensy41_Socket"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "09244b6f-8554-470f-bb66-4338f396f395")
		(at 50 18 90)
		(descr "Teensy 4.1 on two 1x24 standard 0.1 in female headers (P110), rows 15.24 mm apart. Pad n = Teensy edge pin n: 1 GND at the USB end, 2-14 = pins 0-12, 15 3V3, 16-24 = pins 24-32, 25-33 = pins 33-41, 34 GND, 35-45 = pins 13-23, 46 3V3, 47 GND, 48 VIN. confirm - not measured: row spacing and body outline from PJRC's 2.4 x 0.7 in; caliper the Teensy and the headers in hand (guide A3). 3D: XenGi's Teensy_4.1_Assembly.STEP (MIT) via RX7_MODELS, rotated onto the socket from the XenGi footprint's frame (pad 1 at -29.21,7.62) - alignment confirm")
